PART 5 — TRAIN ON MANY PCS
========================================

21. Many PCs — What It Is

Many PCs train ONE model together.

PC 1 ─┐
PC 2 ─┼─ train together → one model → one checkpoint
PC 3 ─┘

Each PC trains on a different part of the data.
After every step all PCs share what they learned, so every PC has the same model.

It is NOT:

PC 1 trains alone
PC 2 trains alone
↓
join the .pt files

PC 1 is the main PC. It saves "best.pt" and the run summary.

Full details: ored\model\docs\distributed-training.md

---

22. Before You Start — On EVERY PC

Do steps 1 to 6 on every PC.

Every PC must show the same version:

RUN

git log --oneline -1

OUTPUT

Same on all PCs.

Make the same training data on every PC (same command, same numbers):

RUN

python scripts\generate_facts.py --repeats 20

If one PC has different data or a different config, training stops and says which PC is different.

---

23. Connect the PCs

All PCs must reach each other.

Same home / same network → use PC 1's normal IP.

Different homes → install Tailscale on every PC and log in with the same account. Use PC 1's Tailscale IP (starts with 100.).

Find PC 1's IP (run on PC 1):

RUN

tailscale ip -4

or:

ipconfig

Allow Python through Windows Firewall on every PC.

Tick "Private" only. Do NOT tick "Public".

Never open these ports on your router.

---

24. Check the PCs Can Talk

Run on EVERY PC. Only NODE_RANK changes.

PC 1 = 0, PC 2 = 1, PC 3 = 2, and so on.

RUN

set MASTER_ADDR=100.64.0.1
set MASTER_PORT=29500
set NNODES=3
set NPROC_PER_NODE=1
set NODE_RANK=0

python scripts\distributed.py launch test --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --session net-check --rendezvous static

(Change 100.64.0.1 to PC 1's IP. Change NODE_RANK on each PC.)

OUTPUT (on PC 1)

  OK   all ranks discovered 3 of 3
  OK   all ranks connected (all-gather)
  OK   all-reduce sum 6, expected 6
  OK   barrier
VERIFIED: every worker can train together

If it waits and never finishes → one PC can't reach PC 1. Check the IP and the firewall.

If a PC has Wi-Fi and Ethernet and Tailscale, tell it which one to use:

set GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME=Tailscale

---

25. Train on Many PCs

Set your Supabase keys on EVERY PC (same as step 9):

set ORED_SB_URL=https://xoauguhlxjozpvukjtro.supabase.co
set ORED_SB_SERVICE_KEY=YOUR_SECRET_KEY

Then run on EVERY PC. Only NODE_RANK changes.

3 PCs

RUN

set MASTER_ADDR=100.64.0.1
set MASTER_PORT=29500
set NNODES=3
set NPROC_PER_NODE=1
set NODE_RANK=0

python scripts\distributed.py launch train --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --session ored_v3-run1 --rendezvous static --set run_name=ored_v3 --set training.epochs=40 -- --upload --report

5 PCs

set NNODES=5

NODE_RANK = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4

10 PCs (or any number)

set NNODES=10

NODE_RANK = 0 to 9

Nothing else changes.

Meaning

MASTER_ADDR    = PC 1's IP
MASTER_PORT    = port on PC 1 (keep 29500)
NNODES         = how many PCs
NODE_RANK      = this PC's number (PC 1 = 0)
NPROC_PER_NODE = GPUs used on this PC (normally 1)
--session      = name of this training run. Same on all PCs. New name for each new run.
--upload       = save checkpoints to Supabase (needed to continue later)
--report       = show the PCs in Supabase

Start the PCs in any order. They wait for each other.

During training (on PC 1):

Epoch   1/40 | train loss ... | val loss ...  <- best so far

"val loss" is from ALL PCs together, not just PC 1.
"best" is picked from this number.

---

26. Continue Stopped Training — Many PCs

Start all PCs again with "--resume-live" and a NEW session name:

python scripts\distributed.py launch train --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --session ored_v3-run2 --rendezvous static --set run_name=ored_v3 --set training.epochs=40 -- --resume-live --upload --report

OUTPUT (on PC 1)

resumed from      : ...live\checkpoint_epoch_0020_... (end of epoch 20, step ...), saved by 3 workers

You can continue with a different number of PCs. Just change NNODES.

3 PCs before → 2 PCs now = OK

OUTPUT

worker count changed (3 -> 2): model and optimizer restored ...

If it says "can only resume with 3 workers" → use 3 PCs again.
(This happens only if you used "--live-every-steps".)

---

27. If One PC Crashes

PC crashes
   ↓
other PCs stop with an error
   ↓
last "live" is safe
   ↓
start all PCs again (step 26)

Nothing is lost except the time since the last "live".

A checkpoint is only used if EVERY PC saved its part. Half-saved checkpoints are never used.

---

28. Add Another PC

1. Do step 22 on the new PC.
2. Stop training (Ctrl + C on all PCs).
3. Start again (step 26) with NNODES one bigger.

Example: 3 PCs → 4 PCs

set NNODES=4

New PC: set NODE_RANK=3

