32. Checkpoint Structure — Many PCs

checkpoints/
│
└── ored_v3/
    ├── best.pt          ← for asking questions (PC 1)
    ├── live.json        ← which live is current
    ├── best.json        ← which best is current
    ├── live/
    │   └── checkpoint_epoch_0040_step_..._1a2b3c4d/
    │       ├── manifest.json
    │       ├── __0_0.distcp    ← PC 1's part
    │       ├── __1_0.distcp    ← PC 2's part
    │       ├── __2_0.distcp    ← PC 3's part
    │       ├── rank-00000.pt
    │       ├── rank-00001.pt
    │       └── rank-00002.pt
    ├── best/
    ├── history/
    └── base/

One folder = one checkpoint, made of all PCs' parts.

"manifest.json" lists every part. No manifest = not finished = never used.

---

33. Important — Many PCs

Always add "--upload". Each PC only keeps its own part. To continue, every PC needs every part, and "--upload" is how they get it.

Use "--rendezvous static" and set NODE_RANK, so PC 1 is always the main PC.

Use a new "--session" name every time you start.

The slowest PC sets the speed. A very slow GPU slows everyone. Leave it out.

Each PC uses batch size 32. With 3 PCs, one step = 32 x 3 = 96 examples.

Windows uses "gloo". Do not set backend to "nccl" on Windows.
